+ *
+ * Every device needs its *own* adapter, because Windows selects a source
+ * address per interface rather than per route: with two virtual IPs on one
+ * adapter it hands the first one to every destination, and the second tunnel's
+ * packets then match none of its policies and are dropped by libipsec.
+ *
+ * Slot 0 keeps the original name and GUID, so the adapter an earlier run left
+ * behind -- and the network profile Windows derived from it -- is reused
